  "suggestions": {"U":"The interface shall support the following user roles: (1) 'emulation end user', defined as a human operator who initiates and monitors emulation sessions via the GUI; (2) 'emulation supplier', defined as an external software vendor that delivers emulation models conforming to the Model Interface Specification v2.1.","A":"The interface shall provide distinct functionality for two mutually exclusive roles: 'emulation end user' (authenticated human operator initiating emulation runs) and 'emulation supplier' (authenticated API client uploading model binaries and metadata).","C":"Keep unchanged — no evidence of factual inaccuracy; however, correctness depends on traceability to stakeholder agreements not provided here.","V":"The interface shall allow an emulation end user to initiate a session via the 'Start Emulation' button (ID: btn-start-emulate) and receive real-time status updates within ≤500 ms; the interface shall accept model uploads from an emulation supplier via HTTPS POST to /api/v1/models with a valid JWT signed by the Supplier CA, returning HTTP 201 on success."},
